course: dictionary
lesson: 8283
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rip is a word with several meanings, so context decides which one you need. Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence. Is something being torn, is water pulling someone out to sea, or is it on a grave? «In Liverpool, Reece lives with his nan in a small house with a ripped sofa, so he never invites his mate Jory back.» Ripped here means torn, because a sofa cannot be a sea current.
explain: Rip is also a noun: a rip is a long tear in cloth or paper. A rip current is different. It is a strong current that flows away from the shore, out to sea. «A rip current is a strong current that flows away from the shore.» Here the word rip is about water, not paper.
explain: Knowing the meaning can keep you safe. «If a rip current carries you, you should float, signal for help or swim parallel to the shore, not straight against it.» A rip is usually narrow, so swimming sideways for a short way gets you out of it. Swimming straight against it wears you out, like running the wrong way on a moving walkway.
fact: Rip can be a verb: to rip is to tear something quickly and roughly.
fact: To rip off or out means to pull something away quickly.
fact: A rip current is a strong current flowing out to sea from a beach.
fact: RIP is short for «rest in peace», written on graves.
fact: «Rip-off» is informal and means a cheat, like charging far too much for something.
exercise: «He wanted to rip the paper in half.» What does rip mean here? | To fold something neatly | To count the pages slowly | *To tear something quickly and roughly | To glue something back together
exercise: «If a rip carries you out, stay calm and float.» What is a rip in this sentence? | A tall wave that crashes on the sand | A quiet pool in the rocks | *A strong current flowing out to sea from a beach | A sandcastle built by children
exercise: «In Liverpool, Reece lives in a small house with a ripped sofa.» What does ripped mean here? | Very soft and warm | Painted bright red | Brand new and shiny | *Torn
test: «The sign on the grave said RIP.» What does RIP stand for? | Run in park | *Rest in peace | Round in pieces | Ready in place
test: Jayden says the ticket price was a rip-off. What does rip-off mean? | A long tear in cloth | A strong current at the beach | *Charging far too much, a cheat | A quick swim to the rocks
exam: «If you are caught in a rip, what should you do?» | Panic and shout without floating | *Float, stay calm and swim parallel to the shore | Fight it hard and swim straight back to the shore | Dive down to the bottom
